# Build/vendor artifacts the checkpoint byte guard must not count: the CEF
# SDK the Windows fetch drops in, the drop directory for the cross-built
# WezTerm executables, and the WezTerm host's vendored third-party dep tree
# (freetype/cairo/libpng/harfbuzz...). None of it changes during agent work,
# and counting it pushed the workspace past the guard's 512MiB ceiling.
.cef-windows/
.cef-test/
prebuilt/
packages/plugins/native-terminal/wezterm/deps/
packages/plugins/native-terminal/wezterm/target/

# Session scratch and crash evidence — MEASURED as the cause of a real
# `checkpoint incomplete (pre_tool)`: one minidump under .btmp/dumps was 467MB,
# ten of them 4.68GB, and the capture took only 146 files before it blew the
# 512MiB byte guard. None of it is source, none of it changes during agent work,
# and all of it is regenerable.
.btmp/
.bmp/
.bttmp/
node-compile-cache/
*.dmp

